    "created_at": "2024-11-06T19:23:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-06T19:23:31Z",
    "body": "What if we assumed that `adoptedstylesheets=\"/foo.css\"` was instead a reference to a genuine, regular (CSS) module, and that modules in general were extended to also support inline modules, which I take as potentially implied by this [comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10673#issuecomment-2430625679)?\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<my-element> \r\n  <template shadowrootmode=\"open\" adoptcssmodule=\"(a module specifier)\"> \r\n    <!-- ... --> \r\n  </template> \r\n</my-element>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen both an inline module and a network-resourced module would be referenceable, by definition.",
